# ── Build context hygiene ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `fly deploy` uploads this whole directory before the image is built, and the
# Dockerfile does `COPY . .`. Two things were wrong here until 2026-07-10:
#
#  1. `.worktrees/` (nine full checkouts, each with its own node_modules) is 4.2GB.
#     Every deploy shipped a 2.76GB context and took >10 minutes, which is what the
#     "Fly's depot builder hangs" folklore in deploy.sh was actually describing.
#
#  2. A bare `.env` line matches ONLY the root .env — NOT `.worktrees/*/.env`.
#     Six worktree .env files (live Stripe keys, prod DATABASE_URL, Fly + GoDaddy
#     tokens) were therefore baked into every production image. Patterns for
#     secrets must be `**/.env`, never `.env`.
#
# Keep this file honest: anything not needed to run `npm run build` should be here.
.worktrees
**/node_modules
node_modules
dist
.git
.gitignore

# Secrets — `**/` matters. See note 2 above.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

.DS_Store
*.log
*.dump
*.sql.gz
clubos_backup.sql
sync-output.log
.fly
fly.toml.bak

# Local-only preview harnesses (warehouse-dashboard.tsx/warehouse-scan.tsx, group-vehicles.tsx; no runtime role).
preview

# ── attached_assets: 203MB uploaded to use 432KB of it ───────────────────────
# Added 2026-08-27, after a deploy stalled part-way through uploading this
# directory and sat at 0% CPU for twenty minutes.
#
# `attached_assets/` is the Replit-era upload dump. The client reaches it through
# the `@assets` vite alias, and exactly TWO files in the entire tree are imported
# — both logos, 432KB together. The other 202MB has been going up on every
# deploy since the folder existed, which is the real remainder of the "Fly's
# depot builder hangs" folklore this file already half-fixed by excluding
# .worktrees.
#
# 🔴 It must be `attached_assets/*`, not `attached_assets`. Docker cannot
# re-include a file from a directory that was itself excluded, so a bare
# directory rule would silently drop both logos and fail the build at the vite
# step.
#
# Re-check the list before adding an import from @assets:
#   grep -rhoE '@assets/[^")]+' --include="*.ts" --include="*.tsx" client/src | sort -u
attached_assets/*
!attached_assets/CUFC_LOGO_1772823768518.png
!attached_assets/Untitled_design_-_2026-04-10T083202.470_1775766890766.png
